{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"a5910d6103986b76","name":"card_event_new_doctrine","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Japan/Legions/events/card_event_new_doctrine","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"NEW DOCTRINE","text":"Ignore \"Cannot attack the enemy HQ\" on target unit.","flavorText":"In 1945 the Japanese were losing control in the Pacific and their tactic was to take up defensive positions in the islands of the Pacific. In Iwo Jima and Okinawa their tactic was to build an elaborate system of underground tunnels and heavily fortified bunkers, and instead of attacking the Americans when they landed on the beaches, they did their best to conceal their positions, both from land and air. The Japanese knew that these battles could not be won, but their goal was to slow down the American advance and bleed their forces, giving them time to build up defenses in the Japanese homeland where they believed a final and decisive battle would take place. These tactics were effective and resulted in two of the bloodiest battles of the war, which nevertheless ended with the total annihilation of the defending forces.","faction":"Japan","type":"order","rarity":"Common","cost":1,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_event_new_doctrine","title":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_event_new_doctrine_title","SourceString":"NEW DOCTRINE","LocalizedString":"NEW DOCTRINE"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::order","faction":"EFactionEnum::Japan","kredits":1,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_event_new_doctrine_text","SourceString":"Ignore \"Cannot attack the enemy HQ\" on target unit.","LocalizedString":"Ignore \"Cannot attack the enemy HQ\" on target unit."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_event_new_doctrine_history","SourceString":"In 1945 the Japanese were losing control in the Pacific and their tactic was to take up defensive positions in the islands of the Pacific. In Iwo Jima and Okinawa their tactic was to build an elaborate system of underground tunnels and heavily fortified bunkers, and instead of attacking the Americans when they landed on the beaches, they did their best to conceal their positions, both from land and air. The Japanese knew that these battles could not be won, but their goal was to slow down the American advance and bleed their forces, giving them time to build up defenses in the Japanese homeland where they believed a final and decisive battle would take place. These tactics were effective and resulted in two of the bloodiest battles of the war, which nevertheless ended with the total annihilation of the defending forces.","LocalizedString":"In 1945 the Japanese were losing control in the Pacific and their tactic was to take up defensive positions in the islands of the Pacific. In Iwo Jima and Okinawa their tactic was to build an elaborate system of underground tunnels and heavily fortified bunkers, and instead of attacking the Americans when they landed on the beaches, they did their best to conceal their positions, both from land and air. The Japanese knew that these battles could not be won, but their goal was to slow down the American advance and bleed their forces, giving them time to build up defenses in the Japanese homeland where they believed a final and decisive battle would take place. These tactics were effective and resulted in two of the bloodiest battles of the war, which nevertheless ended with the total annihilation of the defending forces."},"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Common","selectTargetOnPlayedFromHand":true,"cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::Legions","isReserved":true,"usedTriggers":["ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardSuppressed"],"soundEnterPlay":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'War_UI_Drum_Movement_Taiko_Hits_3'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/War_UI/Waves/Drum_Movements/War_UI_Drum_Movement_Taiko_Hits_3.0"},"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/Japan/Invasion/t_japan_order_air.t_japan_order_air","SubPathStri